ns despite constitutional symptoms", "Metabolic/endocrine crisis: Glucose is normal, no acute diabetic decompensation features", "Autoimmune disorder: Not ruled out but less prioritized without specific markers"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia with blasts", "Uncharacterised neurological deficits (visual changes, ataxia)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.033, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.3751774765131558, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms and blasts are nonspecific for lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorders but do not exclude them; evidence is modest."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of lymphoid lineage markers reduces probability of ALL but does not exclude it entirely in early presentations."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.29409005628517826, "posterior": 0.3683396130977459, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Subacute presentation without chronic MPN history weakens the blast crisis hypothesis, favoring de novo AML as the primary concern."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.65, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urgency", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.167, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of monoclonal gammopathy or plasma cell infiltration significantly reduces the likelihood of multiple myeloma."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.056, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (B-cell lineage)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3041979539295858, "posterior": 0.3041979539295858, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (T-cell lineage)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.050699658988264305, "posterior": 0.050699658988264305, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B2.3": {"id": "B2.3", "label": "Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (Non-leukemic Blast Crisis)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.020279863595305724, "posterior": 0.020279863595305724, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.25, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia"]}}, "frontier": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3", "B3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% blasts in peripheral blood with leukocytosis and pancytopenia support chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm in blast crisis as a viable differential?", "summary": "Blast crisis of CML is possible but weakened by the lack of chronic MPN history and subacute presentation, which favors de novo AML over a transformation."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss, night sweats) and pancytopenia with blasts in peripheral blood support lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorder as a potential cause?", "summary": "Constitutional symptoms and blasts are nonspecific for lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorders but do not exclude them; evidence is modest."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of evidence for lymphoid lineage markers in peripheral blood blasts rule out lymphoid neoplasm (e.g., ALL) as a dangerous but low-probability consideration?", "summary": "Lack of lymphoid lineage markers reduces probability of ALL but does not exclude it entirely in early presentations."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset of symptoms (days) and lack of prior chronic myeloproliferative disorder history argue against CML in blast crisis compared to de novo AML?", "summary": "Subacute presentation without chronic MPN history weakens the blast crisis hypothesis, favoring de novo AML as the primary concern."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of monoclonal gammopathy, Bence Jones proteinuria, or plasma cell infiltration in the vignette disfavor multiple myeloma as a diagnostic consideration?", "summary": "Lack of monoclonal gammopathy or plasma cell infiltration significantly reduces the likelihood of multiple myeloma."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence is MOST INCONSISTENT with Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts? Identify the single strongest finding that argues against this diagnosis.", "summary": "No single finding strongly contradicts myeloid neoplasm; pancytopenia and blasts remain consistent with AML or MDS."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B2", 0.375], ["B3", 0.368], ["B2.1", 0.304]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers (airway/breathing compromise, shock, altered mental status with instability, or uncontrolled hemorrhage) are present. Hematologic abnormalities (blasts, anemia, thrombocytopenia) and neurological deficits are non-focal and subacute, not requiring urgent stabilization before diagnostic clarification.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading branch (B3: Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm) has posterior 0.368 < 0.75, and dangerous alternatives (B2: Lymphoid Neoplasm with posterior 0.375) remain unresolved. Estimated_remaining_value exceeds 0.1, and further discriminators (e.g., lineage-specific markers, bone marrow biopsy) are untried but available."}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.353, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.3683396130977459, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Multiple myeloma'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B2", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.375}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "posterior": 0.368, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 3, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Subacute presentation without chronic MPN history weakens the blast crisis hypothesis, favoring de novo AML as the prim…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 1, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B2.1", "B4", "B5"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=71%, source=both]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (B-cell lineage):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, cellular immunodeficiency\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (T-cell lineage):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, cellular immunodeficiency\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (Non-leukemic Blast Crisis):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, cellular immunodeficiency, chronic lymphatic leukemia\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (B-cell lineage):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (T-cell lineage):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (Non-leukemic Blast Crisis):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, cellular immunodeficiency, somatic mutation\n\nAcute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (B-cell lineage) vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (Non-leukemic Blast Crisis):\n  Favours first:  balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain, enlarged liver\n\nAcute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (T-cell lineage) vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (Non-leukemic Blast Crisis):\n  Favours first:  balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain, enlarged liver\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm: bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\nRelated to Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (B-cell lineage): acute lymphoblastic leukemia (disease), acute lymphoblastic/lymphocytic leukemia, childhood leukemia\n\nRelated to Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (T-cell lineage): acute lymphoblastic leukemia (disease), acute lymphoblastic/lymphocytic leukemia, childhood leukemia\n\nRelated to Lymphoblastic Lymphoma (Non-leukemic Blast Crisis): non-hodgkin lymphoma, precursor lymphoblastic lymphoma/leukemia, t-cell childhood lymphoblastic lymphoma\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  he experienced a headache with blurry vision → seizure → Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm"}
