lasm (accelerated phase): Lacks chronic features (no prior MPN diagnosis, no splenomegaly on exam)", "Infectious aetiology: Constitutional symptoms without focal infection signs", "Autoimmune disorder: Not ruled out but lacks specific serologic markers", "Metabolic/endocrine crisis: Normal glucose and electrolytes"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional alarm signs (fever, weight loss, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia with blasts", "Neurological deficits (visual acuity decline, ataxia)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2703584764749813, "posterior": 0.2703584764749813, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.6488603435399551, "posterior": 0.6488603435399551, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.65, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urgency", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.057, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.077, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.043, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% blasts in peripheral blood and constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) align with CML in blast crisis as a plausible chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm variant?", "summary": "The blast count aligns with CML in blast crisis (a sub-entity of B3), but the lack of chronic MPN history (e.g., prior diagnosis, splenomegaly) weakens this explanation."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented splenomegaly or prior BCR-ABL1 testing (no chronic MPN history) argue against CML in blast crisis as a differential within the myeloid neoplasm category?", "summary": "Absence of splenomegaly (a common feature in CML blast crisis) and no chronic MPN history reduces support for CML in blast crisis (B3 sub-entity), but does not exclude other myeloid neoplasms."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's subacute onset without chronic MPN history (e.g., no splenomegaly, no prior MPN diagnosis) argue against a chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm in accelerated phase as the primary d…", "summary": "Subacute presentation without chronic MPN features (e.g., prior MPN diagnosis, splenomegaly) makes accelerated-phase MPN (B3 sub-entity) less likely, but does not eliminate other MPN variants."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% peripheral blasts with subacute constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) and neurological findings (visual acuity decline, ataxia) argue for de novo AML as the most dange…", "summary": "A 35% blast count is highly suggestive of acute myeloid leukemia (B1), which is a dangerous condition requiring immediate evaluation. Constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) further support this over chronic myeloproliferative origins."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 35% blast count in peripheral blood, combined with constitutional symptoms but absence of chronic MPN markers (no splenomegaly, no prior MPN history), represent a transitional phase between …", "summary": "The lack of chronic MPN features (e.g., splenomegaly, prior MPN history) argues against CML in blast crisis (B3 sub-entity) as a transitional phase, though isolated blast counts alone don't rule out de novo myeloid neoplasms."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the complete absence of chronic MPN features (no prior BCR-ABL1 testing, no splenomegaly, no documented MPN history) make CML in blast crisis less likely than de novo AML despite the high blast …", "summary": "Without evidence of prior chronic myeloproliferative disease or splenomegaly, CML in blast crisis (B3) becomes less likely, and de novo AML (B1) remains the more dangerous explanation for the blast count and systemic symptoms."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.286], ["B2", 0.248], ["B2.1", 0.176]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.552], ["B2", 0.298], ["B4", 0.148]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.663], ["B2", 0.19], ["B4", 0.094]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers present", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading branch B3 posterior (0.663) remains below 0.75 threshold. Dangerous alternatives (B1 danger=0.9, B2 danger=0.85) with posterior ≥0.10 still exist. Available discriminators (bone marrow biopsy, flow cytometry) could significantly alter management decisions."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.9, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.6634715449337274, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Multiple myeloma', 'Chronic myelogenous leukemia', 'Myeloproliferative disorder', 'splenomegaly'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B2", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.375}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "posterior": 0.649, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 1}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 3, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1", "B4", "B2"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=60%, source=primekg]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase) vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase): bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
